<section>
    <h3>What to bring</h3>
    <p>You need to show:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Your child's medical book from the hospital or birthing centre (sometimes called the green book or
            immunisation book).</li>
        <li>A valid form of photo identification for each parent who will be named on the birth record.</li>
        <li>Your Barbados National ID card, valid passport or other government-issued ID if you are a Barbadian citizen.
            Non-Barbadian nationals must show their valid passport.</li>
        <li>Your original marriage certificate if you are married to the child's other parent.</li>
    </ol>

    <h4>Parents who are minors</h4>
    <p>If you are a mother or a father and you are under 16 years old, you are considered a minor. You must be
        accompanied by your parent(s) or guardian(s).</p>
    <p><strong>If you have a valid passport, you must bring:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>your valid passport</li>
        <li>your original birth certificate</li>
        <li>the child's medical book (green book)</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>If you do not have a valid passport, you must bring:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>your minor's identification card</li>
        <li>your original birth certificate</li>
        <li>the child's medical book (green book)</li>
        <li>an identification letter signed by a Justice of the Peace</li>
    </ul>
</section>

